 # Gaussian Opacity Fields (GOF)
 
+
 ## Overview
-Gaussian Opacity Fields (GOF) [S1] is a radiance field representation that builds on 3D Gaussian Splatting (3DGS) [KKLD23] by replacing the standard 2D projection rasterization with ray-tracing-based volume rendering [S1]. Unlike 3DGS, which projects 3D Gaussians onto the image plane as 2D Gaussians, GOF analytically evaluates the maximum Gaussian contribution along each pixel ray [S1]. This approach provides accurate depth estimation and facilitates the derivation of level-set surfaces from accumulated opacity [S2, unofficial].
